From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: with EDEN_UP_SCALED_ONLY=1, the census and the collector count a freed native copy as freed

What: Image::HostMemoryBytes (vk_texture_cache.h) gives 0 while 0810 has freed the native copy
(only the scaled copy is held, which GetScaledImageSizeBytes counts apart), so
TextureCache::ImageMemoryBytes, the census ("target", "astc", "other", stale and unmapped
fields) and EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS's "images" show what is really held. TextureCache::ScaleUp and
ScaleDown add the change of a registered image's ImageMemoryBytes to total_used_memory, as
BindSparseTiles does for later binds, so RegisterImage's and DeleteImage's counts stay paired.
Why: without it the census keeps showing the full native size of a rescaled target (the cache's
own guess from the guest size, since original_image is empty), so a test could not see 0810's
gain in the census, only in the driver line; and the collector would think the cache holds more
than it does and evict sooner than needed.
Off: one cached test per scale change; HostMemoryBytes's new test reads a bool that is never set
without the switch.
Where the runtime reports device memory (CanReportMemoryUsage), TickFrame sets the total from the
driver every frame anyway, so the pairing matters only within a frame. Not covered: a native copy
made again inside UploadMemory/DownloadMemory and kept there (an image's second return) is not
added to total_used_memory until that frame end; DeleteImage subtracts at most what is counted
(it clamps at 0).

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
index 1b8778d401..6ad558c09a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
@@ -616,6 +616,9 @@ public:
     /// Host memory the image takes, for the texture cache's total (none while unbacked): a
     /// trimmed or converted image takes nothing like its guest size.
     [[nodiscard]] std::optional<u64> HostMemoryBytes() const noexcept {
+        if (native_released) {
+            return 0; // EDEN_UP_SCALED_ONLY: only the scaled copy (counted apart) is held
+        }
         if (!original_image) {
             return std::nullopt;
         }
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index abc7a7fd84..dc0c9b0a39 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -6380,13 +6380,29 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickAsyncUnswizzle() {
     }
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_SCALED_ONLY=1 (vk_texture_cache.cpp, 0810): a scale can free or make again an image's
+// native copy. RegisterImage counted what the image held then; the change is added here, as
+// BindSparseTiles does for later binds. Off: one cached test.
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool ScaledOnlyCounts() {
+    static const bool on = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_SCALED_ONLY");
+    return on;
+}
+
 template <class P>
 bool TextureCache<P>::ScaleUp(Image& image) {
     const bool has_copy = image.HasScaled();
+    const bool count_native = ScaledOnlyCounts() && True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Registered);
+    const u64 held_before = count_native ? ImageMemoryBytes(image) : 0;
     const bool rescaled = image.ScaleUp();
     if (!has_copy && image.HasScaled()) {
         total_used_memory += GetScaledImageSizeBytes(image);
     }
+    if (count_native) {
+        const u64 held_after = ImageMemoryBytes(image);
+        total_used_memory = total_used_memory + held_after >= held_before
+                                ? total_used_memory + held_after - held_before
+                                : 0;
+    }
     if (!rescaled) {
         return false;
     }
@@ -6396,7 +6412,12 @@ bool TextureCache<P>::ScaleUp(Image& image) {
 
 template <class P>
 bool TextureCache<P>::ScaleDown(Image& image) {
+    const bool count_native = ScaledOnlyCounts() && True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Registered);
+    const u64 held_before = count_native ? ImageMemoryBytes(image) : 0;
     const bool rescaled = image.ScaleDown();
+    if (count_native) {
+        total_used_memory += ImageMemoryBytes(image) - (std::min)(held_before, ImageMemoryBytes(image));
+    }
     if (!rescaled) {
         return false;
     }
